H8549.strongs:
Origin: from 8552;
Meaning: entire (literally, figuratively or morally); also (as noun) integrity, truth
KJV renders: without blemish, complete, full, perfect, sincerely (-ity), sound, without spot, undefiled, upright(-ly), whole.

H8550.strongs:
Origin: plural of 8537;
Meaning: perfections, i.e. (techn.) one of the epithets of the objects in the high-priest's breastplate as an emblem of complete Truth
KJV renders: Thummim.

H8551.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to sustain; by implication, to obtain, keep fast; figuratively, to help, follow close
KJV renders: (take, up-) hold (up), maintain, retain, stay (up).

H8552.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to complete, in a good or a bad sense, literal, or figurative, transitive or intransitive
KJV renders: accomplish, cease, be clean (pass-) ed, consume, have done, (come to an, have an, make an) end, fail, come to the full, be all gone, × be all here, be (make) perfect, be spent, sum, be (shew self) upright, be wasted, whole.

H8553.strongs:
Origin: from 4487; a portion assigned;
Meaning: Timnah, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV renders: Timnah, Timnath, Thimnathah.

H8554.strongs:
Origin: patrial from 8553;
Meaning: a Timnite or inhabitant of Timnah
KJV renders: Timnite.

H8555.strongs:
Origin: from 4513; restraint;
Meaning: Timna, the name of two Edomites
KJV renders: Timna, Timnah.

H8556.strongs:
Origin: or תִּמְנַת סֶרַח; from 8553 and 2775; portion of (the) sun;
Meaning: Timnath-Cheres, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Timnath-heres, Timnath-serah.

H8557.strongs:
Origin: from 4529;
Meaning: liquefaction, i.e. disappearance
KJV renders: melt.

H8558.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to be erect;
Meaning: a palm tree
KJV renders: palm (tree).

H8559.strongs:
Origin: the same as 8558;
Meaning: Tamar, the name of three women and a place
KJV renders: Tamar.

H8560.strongs:
Origin: from the same root as 8558;
Meaning: a palm trunk
KJV renders: palm tree.

H8561.strongs:
Origin: (plural or (feminine) תִּמֹּרָה; (singular and plural), from the same root as 8558;
Meaning: (architectural) a palm-like pilaster (i.e. umbellate)
KJV renders: palm tree.

H8562.strongs:
Origin: or תַּמְרֻק; or תַּמְרִיק; from 4838;
Meaning: properly, a scouring, i.e. soap or perfumery for the bath; figuratively, a detergent
KJV renders: × cleanse, (thing for) purification(-fying).

H8563.strongs:
Origin: from 4843;
Meaning: bitterness (plural as collective)
KJV renders: × most bitter(-ly).

H8564.strongs:
Origin: from the same root as 8558;
Meaning: an erection, i.e. pillar (probably for a guide-board)
KJV renders: high heap.

H8565.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root probably meaning to elongate;
Meaning: a monster (as preternaturally formed), i.e. a sea-serpent (or other huge marine animal); also a jackal (or other hideous land animal)
KJV renders: dragon, whale. Compare 8577.

H8566.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to present (a mercenary inducement), i.e. bargain with (a harlot)
KJV renders: hire.

H8567.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (identical with through the idea of attributing honor);
Meaning: to ascribe (praise), i.e. celebrate, commemorate
KJV renders: lament, rehearse.

H8568.strongs:
Origin: probably feminine of 8565;
Meaning: a female jackal
KJV renders: dragon.

H8569.strongs:
Origin: from 5106;
Meaning: alienation; by implication, enmity
KJV renders: breach of promise, occasion.

H8570.strongs:
Origin: from 5107;
Meaning: produce
KJV renders: fruit, increase.

H8571.strongs:
Origin: perhaps from the same as 594 through the idea of protraction;
Meaning: a pinnacle, i.e. extremity
KJV renders: tip.

H8572.strongs:
Origin: from 5123;
Meaning: drowsiness, i.e. sleep
KJV renders: slumber(-ing).

H8573.strongs:
Origin: from 5130;
Meaning: a brandishing (in threat); by implication, tumult; specifically, the official undulation of sacrificial offerings
KJV renders: offering, shaking, wave (offering).

H8574.strongs:
Origin: from 5216;
Meaning: a fire-pot
KJV renders: furnace, oven.

H8575.strongs:
Origin: or תַּנְחֻם; and (feminine) תַּנְחוּמָה; from 5162;
Meaning: compassion, solace
KJV renders: comfort, consolation.

H8576.strongs:
Origin: for 8575 (feminine);
Meaning: Tanchumeth, an Israelite
KJV renders: Tanhumeth.

H8577.strongs:
Origin: or תַּנִּים; (Ezekiel 29:3), intensive from the same as 8565;
Meaning: a marine or land monster, i.e. sea-serpent or jackal
KJV renders: dragon, sea-monster, serpent, whale.

H8578.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 8147;
Meaning: second
KJV renders: second.

H8579.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from 8578;
Meaning: a second time
KJV renders: again.

H8580.strongs:
Origin: from 5395;
Meaning: properly, a hard breather, i.e. the name of two unclean creatures, a lizard and a bird (both perhaps from changing color through their irascibility), probably the tree-toad and the water-hen
KJV renders: mole, swan.

H8581.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to loathe, i.e. (morally) detest
KJV renders: (make to be) abhor(-red), (be, commit more, do) abominable(-y), × utterly.

H8582.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to vacillate, i.e. reel or stray (literally or figuratively); also causative of both
KJV renders: (cause to) go astray, deceive, dissemble, (cause to, make to) err, pant, seduce, (make to) stagger, (cause to) wander, be out of the way.

H8584.strongs:
Origin: from 5749;
Meaning: attestation, i.e. a precept, usage
KJV renders: testimony.

H8585.strongs:
Origin: from 5927;
Meaning: a channel (into which water is raised for irrigation); also a bandage or plaster (as placed upon a wound)
KJV renders: conduit, cured, healing, little river, trench, watercourse.

H8586.strongs:
Origin: from 5953;
Meaning: caprice (as a fit coming on), i.e. vexation; concretely a tyrant
KJV renders: babe, delusion.

H8587.strongs:
Origin: from 5956;
Meaning: a secret
KJV renders: thing that is hid, secret.

H8588.strongs:
Origin: or תַּעֲנֻג; and (feminine) תַּעֲנֻגָה; from 6026;
Meaning: luxury
KJV renders: delicate, delight, pleasant.

H8589.strongs:
Origin: from 6031;
Meaning: affliction (of self), i.e. fasting
KJV renders: heaviness.

H8590.strongs:
Origin: or תַּעְנָךְ; of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: Taanak or Tanak, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Taanach, Tanach.

H8591.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to cheat; by analogy, to maltreat
KJV renders: deceive, misuse.

H8592.strongs:
Origin: from 6105;
Meaning: might (plural collective)
KJV renders: power.

H8593.strongs:
Origin: from 6168;
Meaning: a knife or razor (as making bare); also a scabbard (as being bare, i.e. empty)
KJV renders: (pen-) knife, razor, scabbard, shave, sheath.

H8594.strongs:
Origin: from 6148;
Meaning: suretyship, i.e. (concretely) a pledge
KJV renders: hostage.

H8595.strongs:
Origin: from 8591;
Meaning: a fraud
KJV renders: error.

H8596.strongs:
Origin: from 8608 contracted;
Meaning: a tambourine
KJV renders: tabret, timbrel.

H8597.strongs:
Origin: or תִּפְאֶרֶת; from 6286;
Meaning: ornament (abstractly or concretely, literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: beauty(-iful), bravery, comely, fair, glory(-ious), honour, majesty.

H8598.strongs:
Origin: from 5301;
Meaning: an apple (from its fragrance), i.e. the fruit or the tree (probably includ. others of the pome order, as the quince, the orange, etc.)
KJV renders: apple (tree). See also 1054.

H8599.strongs:
Origin: the same as 8598;
Meaning: Tappuach, the name of two places in Palestine, also of an Israelite
KJV renders: Tappuah.
